<title>GERMANY: BMW '97 sales could exceed 60 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>BMW '97 sales could exceed 60 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Bayerische Motoren Werke AG group sales could exceed 60 billion marks ($35.57 billion) in 1997, chairman Bernd Pischetsrieder said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Asked at a press conference if it was possible that BMW sales in 1997 could be over 60 billion marks, he said: &quot;The answer to that question is yes.&quot;</p>
<p>Pischetsrieder had earlier refused to offer a specific sales forecast for 1997. BMW had sales of 52.3 billion marks in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($1=1.6868 Mark)</p>
